WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.140
Hey this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.440
A teacher writes six words on the board: cat, dog,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:13.259
has, max, dim, and tag. The teacher hands a

00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:15.690
piece of paper to Albert another piece

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.910
of paper to Bernard and another piece of

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.939
paper to Cheryl. The teacher announces

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.760
that each paper contains a different

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.140
letter from one of the words on the board.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:33.660
The teacher asks aloud, "Albert do you know the word?"

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.240
Albert replies, "Yes."

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:39.200
He does know the word.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.540
The teacher then asked aloud, "Bernard, do you know the word?"

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:51.680
Bernard, after a moment of thinking replies, "Yes."

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.600
He also knows the word.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.340
The teacher then asked if Cheryl

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:01.460
knows the word and Cheryl, after a moment

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.960
of thinking also replies, "Yes."

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.040
She also knows the word.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:12.640
Albert, Bernard and Cheryl always aced their logic exams.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.940
What is the secret word that their three letters spell?

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.500
Can you figure it out?

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.360
Give this problem a try and

00:01:20.369 --> 00:01:21.960
when you're ready keep watching the

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.600
video for the solution.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.840
We're going to analyze the letters in

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:35.689
each of the words in relation to the

00:01:35.689 --> 00:01:39.200
responses that Albert, Bernard, and Cheryl give.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.979
The teacher first asked if Albert

00:01:42.979 --> 00:01:45.470
knows the word and he responds that he

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:48.229
does know the word.

00:01:48.229 --> 00:01:51.020
This means that Albert's letter can

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.120
uniquely identify a word.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:54.820
In other words,

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:57.400
the frequency of the letter that he got

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.040
is exactly one.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:01.680
For example,

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.700
consider if albert had gotten the letter C.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.660
The letter C only appears in the word cat

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.460
so Albert had gotten the letter C he would

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:15.220
be able to figure out that the word is cat.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.400
In contrast suppose Albert had

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.680
gotten the letter A.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:24.680
Well the letter A appears in multiple words,

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.780
so there would have been no way for Albert to figure out

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.680
which word was the word that they got.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.760
Since Albert replied he was able to

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.850
identify the word that means he did not

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:43.010
get the letter A so we need to find out

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.250
which letters appear exactly once in

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:47.400
this list of words.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:53.000
We can go through all of the words and we can figure out which

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.820
of these letters uniquely appear one

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.480
time in this list.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:06.800
These are the letters: C, O, H, or S, X and letter I.

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:13.280
Notice in word tag the letters T, A and G

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.260
all appear multiple times in this list.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.240
So since Albert replied that he could

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.620
identify the word, that means he didn't

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:24.019
have any of these letters. The word

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:26.360
cannot be TAG.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.080
The teacher then asked Bernard if he knows the word.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:37.720
Bernard, after a moment of thinking, also replies

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:40.940
yes so Bernard has heard Albert's answer

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:43.060
and wants to continue

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:47.920
the logic, so from this list of words, and

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:51.670
the letters that are remaining, Bernard

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:55.239
would be able to uniquely identify which

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:57.140
word they all had.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:00.800
so we go through this list.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:04.540
It could be the letter T.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:06.740
It could be the letter G.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.040
It could be the letter H,

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:12.500
if Albert had gotten the letter S also

00:04:12.519 --> 00:04:14.200
it could have been the letter S if

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:18.400
Albert had gotten the letter H. These are

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.130
the possible choices the other letters

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.919
appear more than once in this list of

00:04:23.919 --> 00:04:25.960
remaining letters that Bernard could

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:26.960
have gotten.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:30.320
What this means is that the

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:35.080
word could not be 'max' or 'dim' so we can

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.300
eliminate those words.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.140
Now Cheryl, who has

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:43.460
heard all of these, is then asked if she knows the word.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.600
She looks at her letter

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:48.160
and thinks about what Albert &amp; Bernard

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:50.740
said and also says, "Yes, I can figure out

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:54.160
what the word is." So, continuing the logic,

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.289
one of the remaining letters has to

00:04:56.289 --> 00:04:58.840
uniquely identify the word. Well, there

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.910
are only two letters left there's a

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:02.780
letter A and there's a letter D.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:08.160
The only unique letter left is a letter D because

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:10.720
the letter A appears in both the words

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.690
'cat' and 'has' so Cheryl must have gotten

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:15.639
the letter D and it could not have been

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.620
the word cat or has.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.200
The secret word is 'dog.'

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.780
Albert would have gotten the letter

00:05:24.789 --> 00:05:26.800
O,  Bernard would have gotten the letter

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.680
G, and Cheryl would have gotten the

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.680
letter D. Did you figure it out?

